A: You can use the following code:
if (!$this->permission->check('edit', $data)) {
    $this->session->set_flashdata('error', 'You do not have permission to perform this action.');
    redirect('dashboard/index');
}

This code checks if the user does not have permission to edit the data. If the user does not have permission, it sets a flash data with an error message and redirects the user to the dashboard index page.
You can customize the error message by changing the string "You do not have permission to perform this action." to any message you want.
Remember to replace 'edit' with the actual permission name you are checking for.
Also, make sure to include the necessary permissions check function in your controller.

